{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAE4TqY7JzzKH8gKwEkG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YKKGhewbntStJWL6P7vnza","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/trials/diagnostics/read_ordering_axis.py","old_string":"    Each band is exactly one curriculum phase, i.e. exactly one difficulty decile.\n    Interpolation matters (limit 6): p13 samples every ~45 updates, so its band\n    edges are estimated rather than observed.\n    \"\"\"\n    x = [u for u, _ in t]\n    y = [v for _, v in t]","new_string":"    Each band is exactly one curriculum phase, i.e. exactly one difficulty decile.\n    Interpolation matters (limit 6): p13 samples every ~45 updates, so its band\n    edges are estimated rather than observed.\n\n    ANCHORED AT (0, 0.0). peft initialises lora_B to zeros, so SCALE*(B@A) is\n    EXACTLY zero before the first update -- a fact about the adapter, not an\n    assumption. Without the anchor f(0) clamps to the FIRST SAMPLE's value: 0.395\n    for p13 (u=33), 0.211 for p14 (u=19), 0.446 for p15 (u=38). Band 0's gain then\n    came out understated by 25%, 11% and 26% -- a DIFFERENT amount per arm, because\n    each tracker happened to start at a different update. That is a systematic,\n    arm-dependent bias sitting in the one cell the sep-9 matched pair rests on\n    (item 99).\n    \"\"\"\n    t = [(0, 0.0)] + [p for p in t if p[0] > 0]\n    x = [u for u, _ in t]\n    y = [v for _, v in t]"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":337,"cache_read_input_tokens":335881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":337},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04a