{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAEUCVUZNdbXpE2RjG8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a sharp negative result and it points somewhere specific. Let me record it:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2576,"cache_read_input_tokens":352700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2576},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"416aba06-b692-4aaf-bb63-f7541e2ee9d8","request_id":"req_011CfAEUBxEeUTGKWL3PKXVt"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAEUCVUZNdbXpE2RjG8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QhNgf2D4ebkX5U57GEVe8V","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/trials; cat >> RESEARCH-LOG.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Saturation explains R. It does not explain G. (07:55)\n\nThe saturation account predicts the displacement totals and the `R` ordering. Split\nthe displacement by *which tier* each band trained, and it splits with it:\n\n| arm | displacement into hq deciles (d0–d3) | into vl deciles (d4–d9) | R | G |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| p13 | **4.441** | 3.979 | 0.22340 | 0.38196 |\n| p14 | **0.824** | 4.757 | 0.20748 | 0.36262 |\n\n- **`R` behaves.** hq rows carry BRIGHT's reasoning instruction; p13 put **5.39×**\n  more displacement into the hq deciles and `R` is higher. Consistent.\n- **`G` does the opposite.** vl rows match the general-retrieval format, and **p14\n  put 20% MORE displacement into the vl deciles than p13 did** (4.757 vs 3.979) —\n  and still came out **0.0193 lower on `G`**.\n\nSo the obvious extension of saturation — *more learning on the G-relevant rows gives\nbetter G* — is **false**. Whatever sets `G`, it is not how much the adapter moved on\nvl material. Total displacement still rank-orders `G` across the three arms\n(8.420 > 6.855 > 5.582 against 0.38196 > 0.38126 > 0.36262), but the tier-resolved\nversion anti-correlates, and a mechanism that only works before you decompose it is\nnot one I should be leaning on.\n\nThis is the third time `G` has refused an account that handled `R`: the registered\nLR-phase story went 2/2 on `R` and 0/2 on `G`, both G misses sharing a sign; the\nordering arms both put `G` at or below random; and now the tier decomposition\ninverts on `G` alone. `R` has been explicable all night and `G` has not.\n\n**It does point somewhere, and at something already registered.** p14 trained the vl\ndeciles in bands 0–4 and then ran **500 further updates on hq material**. If that\noverwrote what the vl rows taught, p14 would show exactly this signature: more vl\ndisplacement *spent*, less vl capability *retained*. That is the FORGETTING account\nwritten into `score_arms_by_decile.py` before it was ever run — *\"p14 learned the vl\nrows and then lost them under 500 updates of hq; predicts p14 WORSE than p13 on\nheld-out vl deciles despite having trained them at high LR.\"*\n\nThat prediction now has a quantitative motivation it did not have when I registered\nit, and the eval is the way to settle it: it measures the **final** adapter on rows\nno arm ever saw, which is precisely the difference between what was spent and what\nwas kept. Queued for the moment p15 releases the GPUs.\nEOF\ntimeout 300 python diagnostics/check_log_structure.py --fix 2>&1 | tail -2; tail -1 logs/t15-hard-primed-probe.log","description":"Record the G anomaly and its implication"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2576,"cache_read_input_tokens":352700,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2576},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"a797296a-6c35-46ca-afd9-c7c49b6a7015","request_id":"req_011CfAEUBxEeUTGKWL3PKXVt"}
