{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAEYgekNfVunTxhje3wc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WwQ2CPDzTLkPxLpQohJra2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/trials; cat >> RESEARCH-LOG.md <<'EOF'\n\n## The tier→metric mapping was never measured, and the one contrast that could\n## measure it points the other way (08:05)\n\nThe section above treats \"hq rows train `R`, vl rows train `G`\" as given, and the\nwhole G-anomaly argument depends on it: *p14 put more displacement into the vl\ndeciles and still scored lower on G* is only strange if vl displacement is what\nbuys `G`. So I went looking for where that was established. It is not established\nanywhere. It enters as an argument in `read_p13.py` — hq carries BRIGHT's reasoning\ninstruction, vl carries an empty instruction and matches the general-retrieval eval\nformat — and is used thereafter as if measured.\n\nIt is measurable, from the one contrast that varies the mixture with the filter\nheld off: T3 (hq 0.3593) against the three uniform draws (hq 0.2910).\n\n```\nuniform (hq 0.2910): R 0.21407   G 0.35902     n = 3\nT3      (hq 0.3593): R 0.21161   G 0.36221\ndhq = 0.0683\n\ndR = -0.00246 = -1.21 sigma_R   ->  dR/dhq = -0.0360\ndG = +0.00319 = +1.01 sigma_G   ->  dG/dhq = +0.0467\n```\n\nIf vl rows trained `G`, raising the hq share — which lowers the vl share — should\n**lower** `G`. The observed sign is **positive**, at 1.0σ. So the estimate is null,\nand such sign as it has runs *against* the mapping.\n\n**What this costs.** The \"G anomaly\" I wrote up minutes ago is only an anomaly under\na premise the data does not support; I should not have leaned on it without checking,\nespecially having just spent an hour on item 98, which was the identical mistake —\nan unread premise inherited from `read_p13.py` and carried forward because every\nlater argument reused it rather than re-derived it. Twice in one session, from the\nsame file, in the same direction.\n\n**What survives.** Everything that does not route through the mapping:\n\n- the score facts — p13 0.22340 / 0.38196, T2 0.21776 / 0.38126, p14 0.20748 /\n  0.36262, identical composition, 5.5σ on `R` and 4.3σ on `G`;\n- the displacement facts — totals 8.420 / 6.855 / 5.582, and the band table;\n- the saturation account of *displacement*, which never mentions a metric: at\n  constant LR, easy material is used up and hard material is not.\n\n**What does not.** Any sentence assigning a tier to a metric, including the previous\nsection's reading of `G`. `G` remains unexplained, and it is now unexplained without\neven a candidate mapping to hang it on. `score_arms_by_decile.py`'s limit 1 already\nsays its pool-CE readings are a proxy for `R` and `G` \"not re-established here\" —\nthat limit was better calibrated than my prose, and it stands.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"/workspace/trials/RESEARCH-LOG.md\"); L = p.read_text().splitlines(True)\ni = next(k for k, l in enumerate(L) if l.startswith(\"| 99 | **every band-0\"))\nL[i:i] = [\"| 100 | **\\\"hq rows train `R`, vl rows train `G`\\\"** — used throughout as if measured, and the load-bearing premise of the G-anomaly section written minutes earlier. It was never measured. The one contrast that varies the mixture with the filter held off (T3 at hq 0.3593 vs three uniform draws at 0.2910) gives `dR/dhq = −0.0360` (−1.21σ) and **`dG/dhq = +0.0467` (+1.01σ)** — null, and *positive*, when the mapping requires it to be negative. *Identical in shape to item 98 and from the same source file: a premise inherited from `read_p13.py`, never opened, carried forward because every later argument reused it instead of re-deriving it. Twice in one session, in the same direction — the pattern is that I re-derive NUMBERS obsessively and inherit PREMISES silently.* Surviving: the score facts, the displacement facts, and the saturation account of displacement, none of which route through a tier→metric mapping. Retracted: every sentence assigning a tier to a metric, including my own reading of `G` one section earlier | **a premise used as a measurement** |\\n\"]\np.write_text(\"\".join(L)); print(\"inserted ledger 100\")\nq = Path(\"/workspace/trials/diagnostics/audit_log_numbers.py\"); s = q.read_text()\ns = s.replace('    \"clamped to the first sample instead of to zero\",\\n',\n              '    \"clamped to the first sample instead of to zero\",\\n    \"a premise used as a measurement\",\\n')\nq.write_text(s); print(\"marker enrolled\")\nPY\ntimeout 300 python diagnostics/check_log_structure.py --fix 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Record the tier-mapping retraction as ledger 100"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1595,"cache_read_input_tokens":359637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1595},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"425fcf20-6019-4ccc-8a18-79d43d02664f","request_id":"req_011CfAEYg8Vo2q8MrZsEef98"}
