{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAFBFooRpQVR9KuqpHyD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Status.** p14 landed and the round is closed; p13 is restored, resubmitted, and verified.\n\n**Score-critical state — done and checked:**\n- **p13 retained at round agent-10, S = 0.22340** — best *and* newest. Staged adapter is byte-identical to its trial adapter (`c02215f0…`), validator reports `valid` (1000 updates, 64,000 exposures, 448 tensors), journal clean, nothing changed outside `/workspace/{policy,trials,submission}`.\n- I found and fixed a **lexicographic sort** in `restore_best.sh` that named agent-8 as canonical because `\"agent-8\" > \"agent-10\"` as strings — it would have demanded a needless 32-minute resubmission.\n\n**p14's registered result:** R = 0.20748, G = 0.36262 — below T2 on *both* axes. The DIRECTION branch fired; concentration is refuted at 5.55σ. Hard-first hands back 85% of the filter's entire G advantage.\n\n**The mechanism, after two premise failures of my own:**\n- p15's band-1 gain (2.418, largest in the log) was impossible under a decaying LR, so I finally opened `train_trial.py`. The schedule is `get_constant_schedule_with_warmup(60)` — **constant after update 60**, mean LR 0.695 in band 0 and exactly 1.000 in bands 1–9. Every LR-based claim I'd made since `read_p13.py` is retracted (ledger 98).\n- That *strengthens* the result: four of five matched pairs sit at **identical LR** and the gradient survives (6.56, 3.71, 2.03, 0.67), and decile 0 gains **14.4× more displacement at band 0 on 30% less learning rate** — LR runs the wrong way. At constant LR the mechanism can only be **saturation**: easy material is used up, hard material is not.\n- Then I checked the tier→metric mapping my G argument leaned on. It was never measured, and the one contrast that can measure it gives **dG/dhq = +0.0467, pointing the wrong way** (ledger 100). G remains unexplained.\n- Corrected significance: σ has 2 df, so p13-vs-T2 is **p = 0.188, not significant**. The ordering *axis* (p13 vs p14) is p = 0.031 on R and 0.049 on G (ledger 101).\n\n**Twelve ledger rows this session (91–102)**, four real tool bugs fixed — a tracker writing to a path no reader opens, a verdict computed from six fabricated zeros, an interpolation clamped to the first sample instead of zero, and the sort bug. New guards for each, all injection-tested; audit runs 0 alerts.\n\np15 is at 620/1000, diagnostic-only and committed not to be submitted. Waiting on it for the pinned readings and the held-out functional eval."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1535,"cache_read_input_tokens":379600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1535},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"886ee1b8-190c-480a-856c-65c79fa43059","request_id":"req_011CfAFBEaspE57YoXjHcQqm"}
