{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAFZ5BwfGdt274ZzVWMB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018qETyLwDsSioBGaD7cDn1F","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/trials/diagnostics/read_arms_by_decile.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Reads score_arms_by_decile.py's output. REGISTERED and pinned BEFORE it runs.\n\nWritten 09:00, while p15 is at update 710 and the eval has never been executed --\nno output file exists. Pinned in the log alongside score_arms_by_decile.py so the\nanalysis is fixed before the data, not chosen after it.\n\nWHAT IS BEING TESTED. Three accounts of why p14 scored below p13 on both metrics,\nregistered in score_arms_by_decile.py's header before that tool was first run:\n\n  FORGETTING     p14 trained the vl deciles in bands 0-4 and then ran 500 further\n                 updates on hq material, overwriting them. Predicts p14 WORSE than\n                 p13 on held-out vl deciles (4-9) DESPITE having spent MORE\n                 displacement there (4.757 vs 3.979 -- measured, item at 07:55).\n  LESS LEARNING  p14 simply moved less overall (5.582 vs 8.420). Predicts p14 worse\n                 roughly UNIFORMLY, with no vl-specific deficit.\n  REDUNDANCY     the deficit concentrates where other material teaches least, i.e.\n                 decile 9, which is still unsolved (~0.80) after 900 updates of\n                 everything else.\n\nTHE STATISTIC, and why paired. Every arm is scored on the IDENTICAL held-out rows,\nso the per-row difference cancels row-level variance completely. That matters here\nmore than usual: 2-way CE leaves 76.1% of kept rows below 0.001, so a decile MEAN is\ncarried by a handful of rows and its SE is large. Item 95 was exactly this failure --\na ratio of two near-zero quantities read as a result -- so the primary reading is a\nDISTRIBUTION-FREE sign test on paired per-row differences, which needs no sigma and\nno normality. Row ids are matched explicitly rather than trusted from ordering.\n\nREGISTERED DECISION RULE, fixed here before any data exists:\n\n  * \"p14 worse on vl deciles (4-9)\" means: paired sign test over the pooled vl rows\n    gives p < 0.05 AND the median paired difference has p14 worse.\n  * \"uniform\" means: the hq-decile (0-3) and vl-decile (4-9) median paired\n    differences agree in sign and their magnitudes differ by less than 2x.\n  * \"concentrated at decile 9\" means: decile 9's median paired difference is larger\n    in magnitude than every other decile's.\n  These can all be false at once; that outcome is reported as \"none of the three\".\n\nHONEST LIMITS, stated before the data:\n\n  1. Pool rows are NOT the benchmark. This is held-out pool CE, a proxy for what the\n     adapter learned -- NOT R and G. And per item 100, the tier->metric mapping this\n     log assumed (\"hq trains R, vl trains G\") is NOT established: the one contrast\n     that can measure it gives dG/dhq = +0.0467 at 1.0 sigma, the wrong sign. So a\n     vl-specific deficit here would NOT license a claim about G.\n  2. n=1 per arm. Comparing finished adapters; nothing replicates.\n  3. Deciles are the p13/p14 buckets, and per item 93 they are not ten difficulty\n     levels: decile 9 carries ~72% of batch loss, deciles 0-8 are unordered\n     (rho +0.100, p 0.798). Read as tier gradient + one expensive decile.\n  4. The sign test treats rows as independent. They share a model and a pool; a\n     shared shift moves every row the same way, so p-values are anti-conservative.\n     Reported as descriptive.\n\nUsage: read_arms_by_decile.py [--json PATH]\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDEFAULT = Path(\"/workspace/trials/diagnostics/arms-by-decile.json\")\nHQ_DECILES = (0, 1, 2, 3)          # hq share 0.628-0.959\nVL_DECILES = (4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9)    # hq share <= 0.128\nP13, P14 = \"t13-easy-to-hard-phased\", \"t14-hard-to-easy-phased\"\n\n\ndef sign_test(diffs: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Two-sided exact binomial sign test on nonzero differences.\"\"\"\n    from math import comb\n    nz = [d for d in diffs if d != 0]\n    n = len(nz)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0, 0, float(\"nan\")\n    k = sum(1 for d in nz if d > 0)\n    tail = min(k, n - k)\n    p = sum(comb(n, i) for i in range(tail + 1)) / (2 ** n) * 2\n    return k, n, min(1.0, p)\n\n\ndef median(v: list) -> float:\n    s = sorted(v)\n    n = len(s)\n    if not n:\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    return s[n // 2] if n % 2 else 0.5 * (s[n // 2 - 1] + s[n // 2])\n\n\ndef paired(res: dict, a: str, b: str, decile: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Per-row (a - b) over rows present in BOTH, matched on row_id.\"\"\"\n    ra = {r: v for r, v in res[a][decile][\"rows\"]}\n    rb = {r: v for r, v in res[b][decile][\"rows\"]}\n    return [ra[r] - rb[r] for r in ra if r in rb]\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--json\", type=Path, default=DEFAULT)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    if not args.json.is_file():\n        print(f\"{args.json} does not exist yet -- the eval has not been run.\")\n        print(\"Registered predictions:\")\n        print(\"  FORGETTING     p14 worse on vl deciles 4-9 (paired sign test p<0.05)\")\n        print(\"  LESS LEARNING  hq and vl deficits agree in sign, within 2x\")\n        print(\"  REDUNDANCY     decile 9's median |difference| the largest of all ten\")\n        return\n    d = json.loads(args.json.read_text())\n    res = d[\"results\"]\n    if P13 not in res or P14 not in res:\n        print(f\"need both {P13} and {P14}; have {list(res)}\")\n        return\n\n    print(\"=\" * 74)\n    print(\"HELD-OUT FUNCTIONAL EVAL -- paired per-row, p14 minus p13\")\n    print(f\"held-out rows: {d['held_out_rows']:,}   sampled {d['per_decile']}/decile\")\n    print(\"positive difference = p14 has HIGHER loss = p14 is WORSE\")\n    print(\"=\" * 74)\n    print(f\"  {'dec':>4}{'n':>6}{'median diff':>14}{'p14 worse':>11}{'sign p':>9}\")\n    med = {}\n    for k in range(10):\n        diffs = paired(res, P14, P13, str(k))\n        m = median(diffs)\n        med[k] = m\n        kk, n, p = sign_test(diffs)\n        print(f\"  {k:>4}{n:>6}{m:>+14.5f}{kk:>8}/{n:<4}{p:>9.4f}\")\n\n    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 74)\n    print(\"THE THREE REGISTERED ACCOUNTS\")\n    print(\"=\" * 74)\n    hq = [x for k in HQ_DECILES for x in paired(res, P14, P13, str(k))]\n    vl = [x for k in VL_DECILES for x in paired(res, P14, P13, str(k))]\n    mh, mv = median(hq), median(vl)\n    kh, nh, ph = sign_test(hq)\n    kv, nv, pv = sign_test(vl)\n    print(f\"  hq deciles 0-3:  median {mh:+.5f}   p14 worse {kh}/{nh}   sign p {ph:.4f}\")\n    print(f\"  vl deciles 4-9:  median {mv:+.5f}   p14 worse {kv}/{nv}   sign p {pv:.4f}\")\n\n    forgetting = pv < 0.05 and mv > 0\n    ratio = (abs(mv) / abs(mh)) if mh else float(\"inf\")\n    uniform = (mh > 0) == (mv > 0) and 0.5 <= ratio <= 2.0\n    worst = max(med, key=lambda k: abs(med[k]))\n    concentrated = worst == 9\n    print()\n    print(f\"  FORGETTING      {'SUPPORTED' if forgetting else 'not supported'}\"\n          f\"   (p14 worse on vl at p={pv:.4f})\")\n    print(f\"  LESS LEARNING   {'SUPPORTED' if uniform else 'not supported'}\"\n          f\"   (hq/vl medians same sign, ratio {ratio:.2f}x)\")\n    print(f\"  REDUNDANCY      {'SUPPORTED' if concentrated else 'not supported'}\"\n          f\"   (largest |median| is decile {worst})\")\n    if not (forgetting or uniform or concentrated):\n        print(\"\\n  -> NONE OF THE THREE. Registered as a possible outcome; reported\")\n        print(\"     as such rather than fitted to afterwards.\")\n\n    if \"base\" in res:\n        print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 74)\n        print(\"REFERENCE: frozen base vs each arm (mean 2-way CE by decile)\")\n        print(\"=\" * 74)\n        names = [n for n in (\"base\", \"t02-label-anchor-filter\", P13, P14,\n                             \"t15-hard-primed-probe\") if n in res]\n        print(\"  decile \" + \"\".join(f\"{n.split('-')[0]:>12}\" for n in names))\n        for k in range(10):\n            print(f\"  {k:>6} \" + \"\".join(f\"{res[n][str(k)]['mean']:>12.4f}\"\n                                         for n in names))\n\n    print(\"\\nLIMITS (printed every run): pool CE is NOT R/G, and the tier->metric\")\n    print(\"mapping is NOT established (item 100: dG/dhq = +0.0467, wrong sign);\")\n    print(\"n=1 per arm; deciles are ~two levels not ten (item 93); the sign test\")\n    print(\"treats rows as independent, so its p-values are anti-conservative.\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":392496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":286},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"31ff3d4d-9595-4042-b72f-5dc6d4e64c7f","request_id":"req_011CfAFZ4ZVHeX15Vei5nUE8"}
