{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAG3JipUcHT5tf9Ecn4z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BSc7GbeRE3TWAZ1ZTbtTdL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/trials; cat >> RESEARCH-LOG.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Nearly losing the one replicate in the log (09:25)\n\np15's bands 8 and 9 are the **only replicate of a band measurement anywhere in this\nlog** — the same deciles (1 and 0) at the same bands as p14, after an identical\npredecessor *set*. Every band number elsewhere is n=1, so these two cells are what\nturn \"0.109\" from a point estimate into something with a spread.\n\nChecked the trackers with p15 at update 800, i.e. right as those bands began:\n\n```\ncoarse  16 / 24 samples used   300s interval   ~40 min of budget left\nfine    39 / 60 samples used   120s interval   ~42 min of budget left\np15 needs ~40 min to finish\n```\n\nBoth would have expired within minutes of the finish line, and the samples they had\nleft were being spent *before* the cells that needed them: band 8 had **1** sample\nand band 9 had **0**. p14's corresponding cells have 7 and 9. The replicate would\nhave been measured against almost nothing, and — worse — the final checkpoint at\nupdate 1000, which anchors band 9 and the total displacement, might never have been\nsampled at all.\n\nNothing was failing. Both trackers were healthy, logging, and within spec. The\nbudget was simply sized for a run that finishes sooner, and a `--samples` cap does\nnot announce itself when it binds; it just stops producing rows, which is\nindistinguishable from a finished run.\n\nFixed by **killing the fine tracker and restarting it** with `--interval 90\n--samples 90` on the same file — one writer at a time, because ledger 85 was two\ntrackers interleaving appends into a single `drift.jsonl`. At ~5 updates/min through\nthe hq-heavy tail that is a sample every ~7 updates, so bands 8–9 should land ~26\nsamples against p14's 16.\n\nVerified afterwards: **55 distinct updates, every one with a single consistent\nvalue, zero conflicting duplicates, zero truncated lines.** The restarted process\nhas a fresh dedup set so it can re-emit an update already on disk; the readers\ncollapse by `completed_updates`, and the check above confirms no re-emission ever\ndisagreed with what was already there.\nEOF\ntimeout 300 python diagnostics/check_log_structure.py --fix 2>&1 | tail -2; tail -1 logs/t15-hard-primed-probe.log","description":"Record the tracker budget near-miss"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":931,"cache_read_input_tokens":407681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":931},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"24c8d908-bf70-40b1-9581-fab3922927cf","request_id":"req_011CfAG3JB4zDx2KJUnafQuy"}
