{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAGCBcwMSGUErCdW36Fk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Status while p15 finishes (820/1000).**\n\nThe submission is final and verified: **p13 at agent-10, S = 0.22340**, best and newest, adapter byte-identical to its trial, validator `valid`, accounting exact.\n\nSince the last update I mostly found things wrong with my own work:\n\n- **The matched design is now proven, not asserted.** All three ordering arms have a **byte-identical bucket file** (`06b752da…`), identical seed/method/sources, and distinct phase permutations. That single sentence — \"only the order differs\" — is what the whole 5.5σ rests on, and it had never been checked. Guarded now, injection-tested.\n- **Accounting swept across all nine trials:** every completed arm is exactly 1000/1000 updates and 64,000 exposures, zero problems.\n- **Ledger 101:** σ has 2 df, so my σ-multiples were being read as normal p-values. Corrected — p13 vs T2 alone is **p = 0.188, not significant**; the ordering *axis* is p = 0.031 (R) and 0.049 (G). The distribution-free version (three exchangeable arms landing in the predicted order, p = 1/6 per metric) needs no σ at all.\n- **Ledger 102:** the section headed *\"Kept current so the plan is recoverable\"* was ~15,000 lines stale, still announcing T2 as retained. Rewritten; `check_retained_claim()` now verifies the named arm against the archive.\n- **Ledger 103, a near-miss caught in time:** both drift trackers were budgeted for exactly 7200s and p15 ran longer. At update 800 they had 8 and 21 samples left with 40 min to go — and the cells about to be written are p15's bands 8–9, **the only replicate of a band measurement in this log**, then holding 1 sample and 0. Restarted the fine tracker mid-run at 90s; verified 55 distinct updates, zero conflicting values, zero truncated lines. Budgets now cover 4h.\n\nThat's the third time tonight the failure mode was *healthy-looking silence* — a fix writing where nothing reads (94), an unreached band returning a legal-looking zero (97), and a sampling cap expiring quietly (103). None announced itself.\n\n`read_arms_by_decile.py` is written and **pinned before the eval has any data**, with the paired sign test and all three accounts' decision rules fixed in advance — including an explicit \"none of the three\" outcome. Thirteen tools pinned; audit runs 0 alerts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":798,"cache_read_input_tokens":417221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":798},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"901fe987-ad60-4cfe-8a6b-d3be1a821c45","request_id":"req_011CfAGCB6gFb47GEJmv8tjp"}
