{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAGKpSBsneDmSJH1vzet","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QPr7zbaBL7njxWEZuTmhwC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/trials; python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"RESEARCH-LOG.md\"); t = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"Four of the five matched pairs sit\nat identical LR and the gradient survives (6.56, 3.71, 2.03, 0.67), and decile 0\ngains 14.4× more displacement at band 0 while receiving **30% less** learning rate.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"Four of the five matched pairs sit\nat identical LR. The clean evidence is the **same-decile** contrasts, which hold the\ndecile fixed: decile 0 gains **14.4× more** displacement at band 0 while receiving\n**30% less** learning rate, and decile 9 gives 2.418 at band 1 against 1.460 at band\n9 at *identical* LR. (The monotone trend across matched pairs is **not** usable —\nseparation and decile gap are the same number by construction, item 104.)\"\"\"\nassert t.count(old) == 1\np.write_text(t.replace(old, new)); print(\"RESULT 2 corrected\")\nPY\ncat >> RESEARCH-LOG.md <<'EOF'\n\n## The x-axis was the thing I was plotting against it (09:55)\n\nI spent the session's strongest-sounding sentence on a dose–response: the easy/hard\nratio falling **11.24, 6.56, 3.71, 2.03, 0.67** as the matched-pair separation falls\n9, 7, 5, 3, 1. It appeared in RESULT 2, in `read_ordering_axis.py`, and in three\nsections. Ten minutes ago I *strengthened* it — swapping the sign count\n(P(≥4/5) = 0.1875) for a monotonicity permutation test (P = 2/5! = **0.0167**),\neleven times sharper off the same five numbers.\n\nThen I asked what the x-axis was.\n\nPair `b` compares decile `b` against decile `9−b` at bands `{b, 9−b}`. The\nseparation is `|9−2b|`. The decile gap is `|9−2b|`. **They are the same number.**\n\n| pair | separation | deciles compared | \\|decile gap\\| |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 9 | d0 vs d9 | 9 |\n| 1 | 7 | d1 vs d8 | 7 |\n| 2 | 5 | d2 vs d7 | 5 |\n| 3 | 3 | d3 vs d6 | 3 |\n| 4 | 1 | d4 vs d5 | 1 |\n\nThe mirror design locks them: decile `b` sits at band `b` in p13 and band `9−b` in\np14, so the time gap *is* the decile gap. A monotone decline is therefore just as\nconsistent with **\"more different deciles behave more differently\"** — which is\nclose to tautological — as with anything about time. The trend is reported and not\nused.\n\n**Making a statistic sharper is not the same as checking that its axis means what\nit is labelled.** I improved the test before validating the design, which is the\nwrong order and the more seductive one, because a better p-value feels like\nprogress. This is ledger 87's lesson on the same two arms: that entry killed a\ncrossed-design analysis for a structural reason, spared matched-PAIR readings, and I\ntook the sparing as broader than it was.\n\n**What survives, and it is enough.** Both load-bearing contrasts hold the decile\nfixed, so this confound cannot reach them:\n\n- **decile 0**: 1.578 at band 0 against 0.109 at band 9 — **14.4× more displacement\n  on 30% less learning rate** (mean LR 0.695 vs 1.000). Same rows, same decile.\n- **decile 9**: 2.418 at band 1 (p15) against 1.460 at band 9 (p13) — **1.66×, at\n  identical LR**.\n- **band 0 is uniform**: gains 1.578 / 1.878 / 1.732 across p13 / p14 / p15, a\n  **1.19× spread** over deciles whose base loss spans **53×**. Band 9 across two of\n  those same deciles spans **13.4×**.\n\nSaturation rests on those, not on the trend. The within-pair comparisons also stand,\nsince they hold the band pair fixed; it is only the trend *across* pairs that was\nnever measuring what its label said.\nEOF\ntimeout 300 python diagnostics/check_log_structure.py --fix 2>&1 | tail -2; timeout 900 python diagnostics/audit_log_numbers.py > /tmp/a.txt 2>&1; echo \"alerts: $(grep -cE '\\*\\*\\* [A-Za-z0-9]' /tmp/a.txt)\"","description":"Correct RESULT 2 and log the confound"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1791,"cache_read_input_tokens":425799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1791},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"c3283fcc-ca2b-42b6-9442-8a80878aebca","request_id":"req_011CfAGKowfZh7vkYN7F9XfJ"}
