{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAGaw9S1YrpvrAJPVHqC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014moX82YKwCREbWmCHDn39b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/trials; cat >> RESEARCH-LOG.md <<'EOF'\n\n## What band 0 and band 9 each actually control (10:10)\n\nWith the dose–response withdrawn (item 104), the saturation account rests on two\nwithin-band comparisons. They are not equally clean and the difference should be\nstated rather than glossed.\n\n| band | observations | spread | what it controls |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | p13 d0 **1.578**, p14 d9 **1.878**, p15 d8 **1.732** | **1.19×** | **pure decile** — all three arms have seen *nothing* at that point |\n| 9 | p13 d9 **1.460**, p14 d0 **0.109** | **13.37×** | decile **and history** — p13 arrives having seen d0–d8, p14 having seen d9–d1 |\n\n**Band 0 is clean.** The three arms are byte-identical in kept set, seed and\nexposures, and at update 0 they have trained on nothing, so the only thing that\ndiffers is which decile they are being shown. Their base 2-way CE spans ~53×\n(d0 0.017, d8 0.021, d9 0.907) and their band-0 gains differ by 1.19×. In the\nopening, what you train on barely matters.\n\n**Band 9 is an upper bound, not a measurement.** Its 13.37× confounds *which decile*\nwith *everything seen beforehand*. I should not quote it as a decile effect without\nthat qualifier, and the previous section came close to doing so.\n\n**p15 is the control for exactly this.** Its band 9 trains decile 0, precisely as\np14's does, after the **same predecessor set in a different order** (p15 saw\n8,9,2,3,4,5,6,7,1; p14 saw 9,8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1 — identical as a set). So:\n\n- if p15's band-9 gain lands near p14's **0.109**, the order of what preceded it\n  contributes little, and the 13.37× is mostly a decile effect;\n- if it lands far from 0.109, history-order matters and the band-9 row cannot carry\n  the weight I have been putting on it.\n\nThat is the registered noise cell from `read_p15.py`, and it now has a second job it\nwas not designed for: it is the only thing that can tell me whether band 9 measures\na decile or a history. p15 is at update 860 with band 8 already holding 6 samples\nagainst p14's 7, so the comparison will be well resolved.\nEOF\ntimeout 300 python diagnostics/check_log_structure.py --fix 2>&1 | tail -2; tail -1 logs/t15-hard-primed-probe.log","description":"Log what each band controls"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1714,"cache_read_input_tokens":433496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1714},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ddc471af-9d1d-4e5a-8360-478d04adf2fb","uuid":"7d22b922-543e-473c-922d-1d6167dc0406","request_id":"req_011CfAGav5gBWoM3GyhocJ5f"}
